drm/i915/dp: give full RGB range to a sink that can select it

With Broadcast RGB left at Automatic, intel_dp_limited_color_range()
sends limited range for every CEA mode, such as 3840x2160 at 60 Hz, as
CEA-861 sets as the default. A compositor that asks for full range at
start then changes the pipe's range, which is a full modeset, and a
monitor on the dock drops its picture and retrains at the compositor's
first frame: the screen goes black once at every docked start.

A sink whose EDID's video capability block says its RGB quantization
range is selectable follows the range the MSA or the VSC SDP signals,
so full range shows correctly on it from the start. Give it full range
under Automatic, so the boot's console and the compositor agree and its
first commit changes nothing. A sink that can't select keeps CEA's
default, and Full and Limited still force the range as before.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
@@ -2986,7 +2986,15 @@
 		 * See:
 		 * CEA-861-E - 5.1 Default Encoding Parameters
 		 * VESA DisplayPort Ver.1.2a - 5.1.1.1 Video Colorimetry
+		 *
+		 * A sink whose EDID says its RGB range is selectable follows
+		 * the range the MSA or VSC SDP signals, so give it full range,
+		 * as a compositor asking for it would. Otherwise the first
+		 * commit that asks for full range is a full modeset, and the
+		 * monitor drops its picture to retrain.
 		 */
+		if (conn_state->connector->display_info.rgb_quant_range_selectable)
+			return false;
 		return crtc_state->pipe_bpp != 18 &&
 			drm_default_rgb_quant_range(adjusted_mode) ==
 			HDMI_QUANTIZATION_RANGE_LIMITED;
